cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "qkernel-hep: does the geometric difference predict when a quantum kernel helps? A test on ATLAS H→ττ events"
version: "1.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: Dev Keerthi
    family-names: P
repository-code: "https://github.com/Devkeerthi-code/qkernel-hep"
abstract: >-
  Code, results and report for a test of whether the geometric difference g of Huang et al. (2021)
  predicts how fidelity and projected quantum kernels compare with tuned classical models
  (logistic regression, RBF-SVM, XGBoost) on simulated ATLAS H→ττ events from the Higgs Boson
  Machine Learning Challenge 2014. Four hypotheses written before the experiments are tested over
  Z and ZZ feature maps, 2-14 qubits and a bandwidth sweep, with a noise study, an IBM hardware run
  and a feature-selection robustness check. Tuned classical baselines match or beat every quantum
  kernel, and g does not correlate positively with the quantum-minus-classical AUC gap.
keywords:
  - quantum machine learning
  - quantum kernels
  - projected quantum kernel
  - geometric difference
  - kernel concentration
  - high-energy physics
  - ATLAS
  - Higgs boson
